    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d414-a2">

                <pb facs="0900" n="816" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg816"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 135 <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >bis</hi>.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ministry of
                            State</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName type="venue"><hi rendition="#italic">Palace</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1886-10-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 19, 1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In answer to your excellency’s note
                    of the 11th current relating to tonnage and port dues, I have the honor to
                    inform you that, although all discussion over this matter seems altogether
                    useless, after the proclamation of the President of <pb facs="0901" n="817"
                        xml:id="pg817"/> the United States of the 14th, His Majesty’s Government
                    will he ready to sustain and ratify the spirit of the royal order of 22d June
                    last in regard to this matter, if a settlement of the commercial relations
                    between the islands of Cuba and Porto Rico and the United States can he
                    reached.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>S. MORET.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
